Confluent live round-trip — captured 2026-09-08T07:56:21Z

The point of this file is that nothing here calls /recover. A message is
put on production.events by a script on a laptop; the pri-consumer service
on Cloud Run reads it and drives the recovery itself.

Published via the ingest route instead, the consumer correctly does
nothing: that route already recorded the event in Postgres, so the
consumer sees a duplicate and declines to run it twice. Idempotency
working, and the wrong way to evidence a round-trip.

